Locating the VERIFY.txt hits (a node re-implementation of the gate's own stalePin() logic):
  occurrence 1  line 446  context-ok: true   ("still name the OLD pin 4ca9a071/52 files")
  occurrence 2  line 550  context-ok: true   ("re-pin engine snapshot 4ca9a071 ->")
  occurrence 3  line 553  context-ok: false  ("`README.md` line 4 + line 9 name `4ca9a071` / 52 files")
  occurrence 4  line 554  context-ok: false  ("`CHECKSUMS-slice2.txt` line 2 names `4ca9a071` / 52 files. No commit after 66096fb exists.")

The two VERIFY.txt copies (shipped and prepared) are byte-identical: `cmp` exit 0.

The two causes are different in kind:
  (a) VERIFY.txt:553-554 is a factual report about the DEPLOYED gh-pages tree (which still names
      4ca9a071 because the staged fix is not placed). The gate's correction-context regex does not
      recognise that phrasing. Gate false positive — but SHELL-STATUS.md:53 ("Numerals CLEAN ×2,
      both trees") is therefore not true of the delivered state.
  (b) cakepanz-4-prepared/MERGE-GUIDE.md:3 says "Pin this guide is written against: `5c808472`" —
      the prepared tree's reader-facing guide names the SHIPPED pin and never 65673a00. A real doc
      defect, and the same class Inkling closed at cakepanz-6 in a different file (SNAPSHOT.md was
      fixed there; MERGE-GUIDE.md was not).

Consequence: acceptance-run.sh runs `set -e` and gates at steps 16-17, so the composite would stop
at step 16 on both trees. The delivery states it did not run the composite end-to-end; the
SHELL-STATUS "Numerals CLEAN ×2" line should have been re-printed from a real run.

